malscan was created in the middle of 2018 at RME, a part of the DisCo research group from University of Zaragoza focused on software and systems security.

This is the Volatility 3 port. The original Volatility 2.6 version is preserved on the volatility2-latest branch.

List of contributors in alphabetical order (by surname):

    Ricardo J. Rodríguez
    Daniel Uroz (original author)

